[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186184171,
      "id": "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe",
      "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2b13c024-9808-5e6c-8b41-fb179c75f675",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 11$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4},{b}_{5},{b}_{6}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=11,$ and since $B$ is formed by $6$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 6+\\text{nullity}(A) & =11 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =11-6 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9a6bd676-253a-5b33-b5f5-d171fda96d24",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "b061e1b5-3be6-571a-a294-25a19cd67f41",
